"""Packomania's centres for the rectangle 1 x 0.7, N = 150..330, are not all at a local maximum of the radius, and many
have better packings close by. Local search from the published centres beat the published radius by more than 1e-12
relative for 149 of the 181 N, by up to 5.0e-04 (N = 325): sequential linear programming on the active contacts
(crc.maximize) to convergence, 60 s and 30 s per N of shaking all centres by 0.01 to 1 percent of the radius and re-
maximizing, keeping rises, then maximizing at steps from 1e-2 to 1e-10 of the radius until a whole sweep leaves the
exact radius unchanged, so a fresh crc.maximize pass gains nothing. For the other N the published centres are kept.
These packings are the bar the task scores against. R2 is the exact squared radius of the binary64 centres as
numerator/denominator, COORDS the centres as base64 of little-endian binary64 x y pairs, one string per N. SCiEL run
rect071 (Qwen3.8-27B, from these packings) then raised the exact radius for 132 N, and those packings replace the
earlier ones. SCiEL run rc071 (Qwen3.8-27B, from the packings above) then raised the exact radius for 84 N, and
those packings replace the earlier ones. SCiEL run rd071 (Qwen3.8-27B, from the packings above) then raised the
exact radius for 79 N, and those packings replace the earlier ones. SCiEL run re071 (Qwen3.8-27B, from the packings
above) then raised the exact radius for 34 N, and those packings replace the earlier ones. SCiEL run rg071
(Qwen3.8-27B, from the packings above) then raised the exact radius for 47 N, and those packings replace the earlier
ones. SCiEL run rs071 (Qwen3.8-27B, from the packings above) then raised the exact radius for 63 N, and those
packings replace the earlier ones."""

